sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant TEST as pytest / asyncio
    participant SEL as BsimSelector
    participant CLK as BsimClock<br/>(in pytest)
    participant PHY as BabbleSim PHY
    participant DEV as Simulated Devices

    Note over TEST,DEV: Simulation time = t0

    rect rgb(245, 247, 250)
        TEST->>TEST: Run callbacks and timers ready at t0
        TEST->>SEL: select(timeout to next timer)
        SEL->>SEL: Poll file descriptors with timeout = 0
        alt Callback or I/O is ready
            SEL-->>TEST: Ready file descriptors
            TEST->>TEST: Continue processing at t0
        else Nothing is ready
            Note over SEL,CLK: The standard event loop would block here
            SEL->>CLK: advance_to_us(t1)
        end
    end

    rect rgb(235, 248, 240)
        CLK->>PHY: WAIT(end = t1) via FIFO
        PHY->>DEV: Run timers and RF events through t1
        DEV-->>PHY: HCI, Link Layer, and radio activity
        Note over PHY,DEV: Every registered participant reaches the same barrier
        PHY-->>CLK: Target reached
        CLK-->>SEL: now_us = t1
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 235)
        SEL->>SEL: Poll file descriptors with timeout = 0
        SEL-->>TEST: Ready I/O at t1
        TEST->>TEST: Dispatch I/O, timers, and callbacks at t1
        Note over TEST,DEV: Simulation time remains t1 while ready work is processed
    end

    TEST->>SEL: select(timeout to next timer)
    Note over SEL,CLK: Another WAIT is allowed only when asyncio would block again
